  "prompt": "Compare two scenarios of SCOUT's Quad Cities flood projection, as SCOUT's own flood example does: one with no nature-based solutions in place, and a copy of it with all six. Three shared settings hold the projection period, 2020 to 2040, and the region's top-left and bottom-right corners, SCOUT's example's, which cover SCOUT's whole flood grid. In each scenario, run SCOUT's flood projection with that scenario's solutions, which gives the flood depth and SCOUT's own metrics; take the depth and draw it on its own Autark map in blues, and take SCOUT's metrics, whose median flood depth the comparison shows. Then map how much the depth changes between the two scenarios, as an absolute difference, and show the two scenarios' median flood depth on a pie chart, each value as it is, not combined. SCOUT's flood projection is not part of the standard node set, so whatever provides it needs installing first.",
  "context": null,
